{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"371c7cc03ea954d2","name":"card_event_enemy_spotted","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/Base/events/card_event_enemy_spotted","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"ENEMY SPOTTED","text":"If your enemy captures the frontline, draw 3 cards.","flavorText":"In warfare, spotting the enemy as fast as possible could often mean the difference between life and death. Besides relying on eyesight, troops used binoculars and periscopes, but were also heavily reliant on ground and air surveillance units, plus the radar technology to locate enemies and to predict their next movement. In 1942 US officers commenced special training in recognizing enemy aircraft and ships, using a special technique referred to as the Renshaw Training System for Aircraft and Ship Recognition. Officers studied pictures of planes and vessels and learned to identify them by their form in a fraction of a second. Over a million combined Navy and Army personnel learned Renshaw’s techniques and it is believed to have saved an untold amount of lives during the war.","faction":"USA","type":"gotcha","rarity":"Rare","cost":1,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_enemy_spotted","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_enemy_spotted_title","SourceString":"ENEMY SPOTTED","LocalizedString":"ENEMY SPOTTED"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::gotcha","faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_enemy_spotted_text","SourceString":"If your enemy captures the frontline, draw 3 cards.","LocalizedString":"If your enemy captures the frontline, draw 3 cards."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_enemy_spotted_history","SourceString":"In warfare, spotting the enemy as fast as possible could often mean the difference between life and death. Besides relying on eyesight, troops used binoculars and periscopes, but were also heavily reliant on ground and air surveillance units, plus the radar technology to locate enemies and to predict their next movement. In 1942 US officers commenced special training in recognizing enemy aircraft and ships, using a special technique referred to as the Renshaw Training System for Aircraft and Ship Recognition. Officers studied pictures of planes and vessels and learned to identify them by their form in a fraction of a second. Over a million combined Navy and Army personnel learned Renshaw’s techniques and it is believed to have saved an untold amount of lives during the war.","LocalizedString":"In warfare, spotting the enemy as fast as possible could often mean the difference between life and death. Besides relying on eyesight, troops used binoculars and periscopes, but were also heavily reliant on ground and air surveillance units, plus the radar technology to locate enemies and to predict their next movement. In 1942 US officers commenced special training in recognizing enemy aircraft and ships, using a special technique referred to as the Renshaw Training System for Aircraft and Ship Recognition. Officers studied pictures of planes and vessels and learned to identify them by their form in a fraction of a second. Over a million combined Navy and Army personnel learned Renshaw’s techniques and it is believed to have saved an untold amount of lives during the war."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Basic","isInPermanentPool":true,"usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnFrontlineOwnershipChange"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Class_Specific_Engineer_Socket_Crank_Sequence_2'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Class_Specific/War_UI_Class_Specific_Engineer_Socket_Crank_Sequence_2.0"},"soundAttack":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/USA/t_smiling_subdude.t_smilin